+# Savings and Expense Tracker — v2.0.1 source candidate
+
+**Prepared:** 3 November 2026. **Status: NOT RELEASED; no APK/EXE built or deployed.**
+
+## Financial correctness
+
+- Align planned/actual/forecast cash with dated PF cash transfers without booking them as income or expenses.
+- Keep complete monthly plans; show the current month's comparison as **In progress** rather than a misleading early shortfall.
+- Limit lender settlement quotes/fees/accrued interest to the specified closure month. Other months display indicative principal only.
+- Refuse unaffordable EMI schedules instead of silently inflating the final payment.
+- Keep payment views consistent for legacy undated and before-opening installments.
+- Use one **Unbudgeted spending** label for zero-budget recorded spending.
+- Keep total expenses equal to Living + Debt and savings equal to income − expenses even with legacy sub-paise records, allocating the aggregate rounding residual to one displayed expense group without changing stored entries.
+- Reject fractional-paise new/modified values centrally across categories, overrides, entries, loan balances, payments, PF, provisions, salary history and reconciliation, while preserving unchanged legacy backups.
+- Exclude Asset group from bank reconciliation and recorded totals.
+- Retire inactive daily prorating paths: monthly comparisons use the full-month basis.
+
+## Interface, accessibility and resilience
+
+- Sanitize raw validation/runtime errors in additional UI paths and storage/recovery status.
+- Make chart series follow the selected theme/accent tokens.
+- Render recorded monthly progress as mobile cards at narrow widths; retain accessible desktop tables.
+- Make transaction-grid height adaptive with vh/dvh fallback.
+- Increase tiny supporting text, remove negative-zero money display, and adjust ₹K/₹L/₹Cr rounding thresholds.
+- Avoid duplicate form commits on Enter and ensure Escape cancels an in-progress numeric/text edit.
+- Disclose that future lender-closure dates are indicative, not guaranteed settlement quotes.
+
+## Compatibility and release boundary
+
+- Version staged in package.json/package-lock.json: 2.0.1. Android versionCode derives as 20001.
+- Android application ID remains `com.nandakumar.savingsexpensetracker`.
+- No database or backup format migration was performed.
+- **Original Android keystore was not provided: an in-place signed APK update cannot be built in this environment.**
+- **Windows NSIS installer and full JS/Vitest/Playwright builds were not performed here; npm dependencies were inaccessible (registry DNS failure).**
+- v2.0.0 Drive folder, production website, installed Windows app and Android device are **unchanged**.
+
+See `RELEASE_STATUS_2.0.1.md` for the complete verification record.
